	The function-letter A produces a much more detailed analysis of a
	library than function-letter T, but T is faster.  LFE must scan an
	entire library start block to produce the full analysis A; however,
	LFE scans only the library start block to produce the title analysis
	T.

	Examples

	1.  ) X LFE/L=FAST T MATH.LB CALC.LB <NL>

	2.  ) X LFE T FAST/L MATH.LB CALC.LB <NL>

	3.  ) X LFE/HEX/F T TRIG GEOM INTEGRAL <NL>

	Examples 1 and 2 are functionally identical.  Both command lines
	produce title analyses of libraries MATH.LB and CALC.LB.

	Example 3 produces title analyses of libraries TRIG.LB, GEOM.LB,
	and INTEGRAL.LB.  Because of the /HEX switch, the listing will be
	in base 16; the /F switch ensures that the title analysis of each
	library starts on a fresh page.































